### Guide §5.4 Persistence with JPA. VS Code REST Client syntax: click "Send Request" above each request.
### Start the app with the dev profile, which loads the demo data (5 authors, 10 books):
###   ./mvnw -pl spring-app spring-boot:run -Dspring-boot.run.profiles=dev
### Docker Desktop must be running: Spring Boot starts PostgreSQL from compose.yaml. The console shows
### every SQL statement Hibernate sends, with its parameter values. The ids (Dune is 1) assume the
### demo data on an empty database: reset it with docker compose -f spring-app/compose.yaml down -v

@host = http://localhost:8080

### Since §5.7 every request needs a token: log in as the demo librarian first (200). The others
### send it in their Authorization header
# @name login
POST {{host}}/api/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{"email": "librarian@library.test", "password": "demo-password"}

### The demo books (200, 10 books). Since §5.5 the list is a page sorted by title (08-relations.http)
GET {{host}}/api/books
Authorization: Bearer {{login.response.body.accessToken}}

### Title filter, any case (200: Dune, Dune Messiah). SQL: ... where upper(b1_0.title) like ? escape ...
GET {{host}}/api/books?title=DUNE
Authorization: Bearer {{login.response.body.accessToken}}

### A new book (201). SQL: the exists check (select b1_0.id from books b1_0 where b1_0.isbn=?
### fetch first ? rows only), then insert into books ... (the generated id comes back with it)
POST {{host}}/api/books
Authorization: Bearer {{login.response.body.accessToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{"isbn": "9780547928227", "title": "The Hobbit", "publishedYear": 1937, "totalCopies": 2}

### The same ISBN again (409, detail "A book with ISBN 9780547928227 already exists")
POST {{host}}/api/books
Authorization: Bearer {{login.response.body.accessToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{"isbn": "9780547928227", "title": "The Hobbit (again)", "publishedYear": 1937, "totalCopies": 1}

### Update Dune (200). SQL: a select, the exists check, then the UPDATE on commit: dirty checking,
### the service never calls save()
PUT {{host}}/api/books/1
Authorization: Bearer {{login.response.body.accessToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{"isbn": "9780441013593", "title": "Dune", "publishedYear": 1965, "totalCopies": 5}

### Stop the app (Ctrl+C) and start it again: the data is still there (200, Dune has totalCopies 5)
GET {{host}}/api/books/1
Authorization: Bearer {{login.response.body.accessToken}}

### Emma's ISBN for Dune (409, from the service check; nothing is written)
PUT {{host}}/api/books/1
Authorization: Bearer {{login.response.body.accessToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{"isbn": "9780141439587", "title": "Dune", "publishedYear": 1965, "totalCopies": 5}

### The authors (200, 5 demo authors)
GET {{host}}/api/authors
Authorization: Bearer {{login.response.body.accessToken}}
